<!--meta {"lead": "Compare structured records with real column headers.", "description": "Compare structured records with real column headers.", "variants": "default, dense, sortable, selectable, row actions, sticky, expandable, responsive", "states": "default, hover, focus, active, disabled, loading, empty, error, row hover, selected", "sources": [], "pills": ["Core primitive · derived"]} -->
<section class="ds-section" id="overview"><h2><a href="#overview">Overview</a></h2><p>Compare structured records with real column headers. The customer mocks do not yet show this core primitive. Its roles and states extend the same tokens and interaction rules as the extracted components.</p><p>Use it for this job; choose a different component when the interaction or information hierarchy changes.</p></section>

<section class="ds-section" id="anatomy"><h2><a href="#anatomy">Anatomy</a></h2><div class="ds-anatomy"><figure class="ds-anatomy__figure"><div class="table-wrap"><table class="table"><caption>Appointments</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Braider</th><th scope="col">Status</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Nia Okafor</td><td>Awaiting reply</td></tr></tbody></table></div></figure><ol class="ds-anatomy__list"><li><div><b>Semantic element</b><small>Preserves the native role and browser interaction.</small></div></li><li><div><b>Visible content</b><small>Names the action, value, or status in plain language.</small></div></li><li><div><b>Component class</b><small>Reads shared roles from the token stylesheet.</small></div></li></ol></div></section>

<section class="ds-section" id="variants"><h2><a href="#variants">Variants</a></h2><p>Choose the variant by meaning and context. Keep status or action labels explicit.</p><ul><li><strong>Default</strong> — use this form when the surrounding content calls for default presentation.</li><li><strong>Dense</strong> — use this form when the surrounding content calls for dense presentation.</li><li><strong>Sortable</strong> — use this form when the surrounding content calls for sortable presentation.</li><li><strong>Selectable</strong> — use this form when the surrounding content calls for selectable presentation.</li><li><strong>Row actions</strong> — use this form when the surrounding content calls for row actions presentation.</li><li><strong>Sticky</strong> — use this form when the surrounding content calls for sticky presentation.</li><li><strong>Expandable</strong> — use this form when the surrounding content calls for expandable presentation.</li><li><strong>Responsive</strong> — use this form when the surrounding content calls for responsive presentation.</li></ul>{{example:Base specimen}}<div class="table-wrap"><table class="table"><caption>Appointments</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Braider</th><th scope="col">Status</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Nia Okafor</td><td>Awaiting reply</td></tr></tbody></table></div>{{/example}}</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="sizes"><h2><a href="#sizes">Sizes</a></h2><ul><li><strong>sm</strong> — align height and padding to the sm control role; keep touch targets reachable.</li><li><strong>md</strong> — align height and padding to the md control role; keep touch targets reachable.</li></ul><p>Small, medium, and large control heights are defined by <code>--control-height-sm</code>, <code>--control-height-md</code>, and <code>--control-height-lg</code>.</p></section>

<section class="ds-section" id="states"><h2><a href="#states">States</a></h2><p>The table forces pointer and focus states with <code>data-state</code> for review. Production interactions use native attributes and pseudo-classes.</p><div class="ds-matrix"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Specimen</th><th scope="col">default</th><th scope="col">hover</th><th scope="col">focus</th><th scope="col">active</th><th scope="col">disabled</th><th scope="col">loading</th><th scope="col">empty</th><th scope="col">error</th><th scope="col">row hover</th><th scope="col">selected</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Table</th><td><div class="table-wrap"><table class="table"><caption>Appointments</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Braider</th><th scope="col">Status</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Nia Okafor</td><td>Awaiting reply</td></tr></tbody></table></div></td><td><div data-state="hover" class="table-wrap"><table class="table"><caption>Appointments</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Braider</th><th scope="col">Status</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Nia Okafor</td><td>Awaiting reply</td></tr></tbody></table></div></td><td><div data-state="focus" class="table-wrap"><table class="table"><caption>Appointments</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Braider</th><th scope="col">Status</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Nia Okafor</td><td>Awaiting reply</td></tr></tbody></table></div></td><td><div data-state="active" class="table-wrap"><table class="table"><caption>Appointments</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Braider</th><th scope="col">Status</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Nia Okafor</td><td>Awaiting reply</td></tr></tbody></table></div></td><td><div data-state="disabled" class="table-wrap"><table class="table"><caption>Appointments</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Braider</th><th scope="col">Status</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Nia Okafor</td><td>Awaiting reply</td></tr></tbody></table></div></td><td><div data-state="loading" class="table-wrap"><table class="table"><caption>Appointments</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Braider</th><th scope="col">Status</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Nia Okafor</td><td>Awaiting reply</td></tr></tbody></table></div></td><td><div data-state="empty" class="table-wrap"><table class="table"><caption>Appointments</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Braider</th><th scope="col">Status</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Nia Okafor</td><td>Awaiting reply</td></tr></tbody></table></div></td><td><div data-state="error" class="table-wrap"><table class="table"><caption>Appointments</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Braider</th><th scope="col">Status</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Nia Okafor</td><td>Awaiting reply</td></tr></tbody></table></div></td><td><div data-state="row hover" class="table-wrap"><table class="table"><caption>Appointments</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Braider</th><th scope="col">Status</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Nia Okafor</td><td>Awaiting reply</td></tr></tbody></table></div></td><td><div data-state="selected" class="table-wrap"><table class="table"><caption>Appointments</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Braider</th><th scope="col">Status</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Nia Okafor</td><td>Awaiting reply</td></tr></tbody></table></div></td></tr></tbody></table></div>{{themes}}<div class="table-wrap"><table class="table"><caption>Appointments</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Braider</th><th scope="col">Status</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Nia Okafor</td><td>Awaiting reply</td></tr></tbody></table></div>{{/themes}}</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="responsive"><h2><a href="#responsive">Responsive</a></h2><p>Keep a wide table inside its own horizontal scroll region; for four or fewer columns a page may use cards below 768px.</p></section>

<section class="ds-section" id="theming"><h2><a href="#theming">Theming</a></h2><p>The same markup appears in light and dark themes. Use the semantic roles in the token table; override a component token only for a local variation.</p>{{themes}}<div class="table-wrap"><table class="table"><caption>Appointments</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Braider</th><th scope="col">Status</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Nia Okafor</td><td>Awaiting reply</td></tr></tbody></table></div>{{/themes}}</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="accessibility"><h2><a href="#accessibility">Accessibility</a></h2><h3>Role and keyboard</h3><p>Tab reaches sortable headers, row links, checkboxes, and action buttons in reading order; sorting uses Enter or Space.</p><h3>Focus and labelling</h3><p>Keep the shared visible focus ring. The visible text supplies the accessible name; icon-only actions need an explicit label. Associate help and errors with the relevant control.</p><h3>Contrast, motion, and touch</h3><p>Text uses a 4.5:1 minimum, meaningful controls and focus boundaries use 3:1, and all actions keep a 24px minimum target with comfortable spacing. Reduced motion removes decorative transitions. Check the actual foreground and background pair in both themes on the <a href="../foundations/color.html">Color foundation</a>.</p></section>

<section class="ds-section" id="content"><h2><a href="#content">Content</a></h2><p>Use sentence case. For table, keep the wording concrete and close to the value or action it describes. Show “Awaiting reply” until the braider accepts; label a price estimate as an estimate.</p></section>

<section class="ds-section" id="do-dont"><h2><a href="#do-dont">Do dont</a></h2><div class="ds-dodont"><figure class="ds-do"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><div class="table-wrap"><table class="table"><caption>Appointments</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Braider</th><th scope="col">Status</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Nia Okafor</td><td>Awaiting reply</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><figcaption>Use the table for its stated job: compare structured records with real column headers.</figcaption></figure><figure class="ds-dont"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><span class="text-muted">Unclear action</span></div><figcaption>Do not replace the semantic element with unlabelled text or a decorative shape.</figcaption></figure><figure class="ds-do"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><span class="badge badge--warning">Awaiting reply</span></div><figcaption>Pair colour with an explicit state label.</figcaption></figure><figure class="ds-dont"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span></div><figcaption>Do not make colour or a dot the only carrier of status.</figcaption></figure></div></section>

<section class="ds-section" id="tokens"><h2><a href="#tokens">Tokens</a></h2><div class="ds-table-wrap"><table class="ds-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Part</th><th scope="col">Token</th><th scope="col">Light</th><th scope="col">Dark</th></tr></thead><tbody>{{tok:Color bg surface sunken|--color-bg-surface-sunken}}{{tok:Color border default|--color-border-default}}{{tok:Space 3|--space-3}}</tbody></table></div></section>

<section class="ds-section" id="code"><h2><a href="#code">Code</a></h2><p>Copy the semantic markup and product class; replace the sample content with real data.</p><pre><code>&lt;div class=&quot;table-wrap&quot;&gt;&lt;table class=&quot;table&quot;&gt;&lt;caption&gt;Appointments&lt;/caption&gt;&lt;thead&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th scope=&quot;col&quot;&gt;Braider&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th scope=&quot;col&quot;&gt;Status&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/thead&gt;&lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;Nia Okafor&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Awaiting reply&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre><p>Forced <code>data-state</code> values are for documentation snapshots only.</p></section>

<section class="ds-section" id="sources"><h2><a href="#sources">Sources</a></h2><p>Core catalog primitive. Derived from <a href="../assets/components.css">the shared component stylesheet</a> and the related mock patterns; no direct screen specimen exists yet.</p></section>
